   :criterion-texts
   ["Criterion behavior/pkg12/canonical-signing: Sign the canonical payload binding exact artifact manifest/content, schema, package/version, profile/target, provenance/attestation/SBOM/safety, required recipe, policy level/track, timestamp/log and signer/policy identities; include keyless issuer/subject/audience/certificate/root hashes when used. Check declared key scope and validity; signature integrity alone grants no provenance or consumer authority. Emit canonical payload/hash, signature and secret-redacted verification records. Demonstrate successful verification, content tampering invalidating the signature and refusal of a noncanonical payload, missing required field, wrong subject, out-of-scope/expired key or missing policy-required signing with PKG12001/PKG12002/PKG12003 and applicable identity diagnostics. Consume actual PKG3 manifests, PKG10 provenance and PKG7 recipe evidence; signing does not produce those inputs or independently approve release."],
