   :criterion-texts
   ["Bootstrap criterion bootstrap/stage-equivalence: Actually compare outputs of both named compiler artifacts on pinned source/compiler/stdlib/conformance inputs using every comparison mode declared applicable for that stage: hash, canonical manifest, diagnostic, conformance, runtime output, IR modulo IDs, conditional performance and reviewed accepted-delta. Identify compared artifacts, inputs, outputs, canonicalization and applicable stage support level; emit a provenance-bound equivalence report linked from bootstrap provenance with diagnostic, IR, conformance and accepted/rejected difference records. Fail missing compiler identity/output, unexplained artifact or diagnostic drift, unreviewed or policy-unlinked deltas, failing supported-feature conformance and performance regression beyond a declared acceptance bound when performance is applicable. Preserve stable codes/source spans; permitted metadata/timestamp/wording differences require the declared reviewed comparison policy and cannot hide semantic drift. Retain BOOT1004/BOOT3003/BOOT6003 and BOOT7001-BOOT7007, and exercise both a valid comparison and each applicable refusal. Comparison does not produce compiler executables or independently admit intermediate migration/final release. Required outputs: actual stage comparison inputs/outputs and equivalence artifact; diagnostic/IR/conformance and accepted-delta reports; missing-output/drift/unreviewed-delta/conformance/conditional-performance negative fixtures."],
