   :id "interface/safety/safe1/unsafe-boundaries",
   :criterion-texts
   ["Criterion safety/safe1/unsafe-boundaries: Classify each dangerous operation under active profile/mode/package policy as proven-safe, runtime-checked, rejected or explicit unsafe-island; no implicit fifth outcome or safe-language undefined behavior is allowed. Admit an island only when the policy permits it and the accountable reason/owner/invariant/effects/capabilities/source/generated-origin/profile/target/review metadata and explicit safe boundary or declared absence are retained. Reject forbidden, hidden or unmarked unsafe operations, incomplete mandatory metadata and unsafe behavior exposed as safe without a checked/proved wrapper. Preserve policy-specific audit-only versus review/certificate-required behavior; an internal-only island grants no safe public API. Emit operation classifications, island/boundary/policy decisions and source-bound owning diagnostics with accepted and rejected fixtures; package/release consumers receive the actual records, not inferred compiler success."],
